# MASTER PROMPT: BUILD THE COMPLETE SKETCHTOAPP AI ANDROID APPLICATION

## 1. Your role and mission

Act as a senior Android engineer, full-stack architect, AI engineer, database designer, cybersecurity specialist, Flutter developer, UI/UX designer and DevOps engineer.

Build **SketchToApp AI**, a complete, functional, production-oriented Android application that enables users to transform hand-drawn mobile application sketches and Figma designs into real Android applications using artificial intelligence.

Do not build merely a landing page, static UI, clickable mockup or frontend demonstration. Implement the Android application, backend services, database integration, authentication, AI workflows, design editor, Flutter code generator, build pipeline, artifact downloads and automated tests.

Work autonomously through implementation, testing and debugging. Make sensible engineering decisions without asking me to approve every small detail. When credentials, external permissions or infrastructure are unavailable, implement the real integration boundary, document the exact setup needed and continue with everything that can be completed and tested.

**Primary objective:** Deliver a working Android application from which users can create a project, import a sketch or Figma design, review and edit the resulting UI, generate Flutter source code, compile an actual APK through a secure build service, and download the resulting application.

## 2. Critical architecture decision

This product has two separate outputs:

1. **SketchToApp AI Android application:** The native Android app that users install and operate.
2. **Generated Android applications:** Separate Flutter projects compiled into APK files by the platform.

The SketchToApp AI Android application must not be confused with the applications it generates.

Use native Android development for the main application and Flutter for generated projects.

If the environment supports native Android project generation, use Kotlin and Jetpack Compose. Do not substitute a website for the native Android application.

