## 11. Specialized AI agents

Implement agents as separate backend services or well-defined modules with typed inputs and outputs. They may share the same Gemini model, but each must have a distinct responsibility and testable contract.

### A. Design Analysis Agent
Analyzes sketches and Figma frames, detects components, infers supported layout information and records uncertainty.

### B. UI Mapping Agent
Maps design elements to the canonical schema and supported Flutter widgets. Flags unsupported features.

### C. Code Generation Agent
Coordinates deterministic templates and generates Flutter source from validated application data. It must not blindly accept arbitrary model-generated source as trusted code.

### D. Quality Assurance Agent
Checks schema consistency, missing assets, invalid navigation, unsupported components and likely generated-code problems. Use deterministic validators and actual Flutter analysis wherever possible; AI review is supplementary.

### E. Build Agent
Creates a build job, coordinates the isolated worker, monitors actual build results and associates a validated APK artifact with the correct user and project.

### F. Backend Assistant Agent
Helps explain project configuration, backend integration, authentication and setup errors. It must not have unrestricted access to production data or secrets.

All agents must have bounded inputs, structured outputs, timeouts, error handling, usage limits and observable execution status.

Do not create fake agents that only display decorative status messages.

